## Solitaire Settings in Platinum: $1,180 to $2,445

Solitaires are the most proven style for platinum emerald cut engagement rings. The plain band maximizes the step-cut stone's reflection pattern. Platinum's pure white tone provides the ideal neutral frame for the emerald cut's geometric architecture.

[![Platinum emerald cut diamond engagement ring classic solitaire four prong setting](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-platinum-ring-classic-solitaire.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=all&MetalType=p&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Classic Four Prong Solitaire in Platinum — [$1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (1,815 reviews)

The 1,815 Standard. The most review-validated platinum engagement ring setting in the market. Four prongs, open head, round shank, no embellishment.

The lowest price in this lineup for a platinum solitaire. 1,815 reviews at $1,180 is the clearest buying signal in the platinum ring market.

For emerald cuts: the open four-prong head lets the step-cut table face up fully visible. Add a [1ct IGI F-VVS1 lab emerald cut](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (~$495) for a total ring around $1,675. Add a [1ct GIA G-VS2 natural](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (~$3,000) for a total around $4,180.

**Petite Solitaire in Platinum — [$1,330](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194357?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (1,186 reviews)

1,186 reviews. The petite version uses a thinner band — the narrow platinum shank makes the emerald cut appear larger by visual contrast. The stone is the focus; the band recedes.

For buyers who want the highest review count in the thinnest platinum solitaire, this is the choice.

Pair with a [1ct GIA F-VS2 natural emerald cut](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&colorMin=F&colorMax=F&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (~$3,500) to apply The Color Ceiling. Total ring around $4,830.

[![Platinum emerald cut diamond engagement ring petite solitaire](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-platinum-ring-petite-solitaire.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=all&MetalType=p&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Cable Solitaire in Platinum by James Allen — [$1,550](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/cable-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-315135?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (106 reviews)

106 reviews. The band is a cable twist design — platinum twisted into a rope-like pattern along the shank. The cable texture creates shadow lines along the band that add depth without adding accent diamonds.

Works well with the emerald cut's clean geometry — the organic twist of the cable contrasts with the precise architectural rectangle of the stone.

**Petite Cathedral Solitaire in Platinum — [$1,635](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194270?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (451 reviews)

451 reviews. Cathedral arches on either side of the head elevate the emerald cut stone above the band. Higher elevation means the step-cut pavilion is fully visible from the side.

The cathedral arch also adds prong height, which accommodates larger emerald cut stones without the head sitting too flush against the finger.

[![Platinum emerald cut diamond engagement ring cathedral solitaire](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-platinum-ring-cathedral.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=all&MetalType=p&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Infinity Solitaire in Platinum by James Allen — [$2,105](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/infinity-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-316152?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (50 reviews)

50 reviews at a mid-range price. The infinity band loops under the center stone in a figure-eight pattern before extending toward the finger sides. This creates a distinctive side profile that distinguishes the ring from any standard solitaire.

**Criss Cross Solitaire in Platinum by James Allen — [$2,445](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/criss-cross-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-311128?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (20 reviews)

Two bands cross beneath the center stone before extending toward the sides. The crossover creates a distinctive shadow pattern under the step-cut stone. Buy if the specific design appeals — the review count is low but the design is unique in this lineup.

