## Stone Selection for Platinum Emerald Cut Rings

The same proportion standards apply in platinum as in any other metal: L:W 1.30–1.50, depth 60–64%, table 61–69%. What changes in platinum is the color grade target.

**Color: Start at G, consider F.** In 18k white gold, G color is the practical minimum for a colorless-looking emerald cut. In platinum, The Color Ceiling means F color shows more visible improvement over G than it does in white gold. If budget allows, [browse F-color GIA emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&colorMin=F&colorMax=F&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and compare prices to G. The F-to-G price gap at 1ct is typically 10–20% — worth evaluating before committing to G.

**Clarity: VS2 minimum.** The emerald cut's step-cut table is an open mirror. Inclusions visible in the table are visible regardless of what metal the ring is in. VS2 is the floor. VS1 is the practical recommendation for stones above 1.5ct where the larger table increases the visibility of anything in the clarity range.

**Carat: 1ct+ recommended.** Below 1ct, the step-cut facets are too small for the full hall-of-mirrors effect. At 1ct (approximately 6.5mm × 4.5mm), the stone fills a platinum solitaire band comfortably. Check the [complete emerald cut size chart](/emerald-cut-diamond-size-chart) for mm dimensions by carat weight.

> **Farzana says:** "The stone selection rule for platinum is simple: same proportions, higher color target. Everything else — L:W, depth, table — stays the same as any metal. The only change is the Color Ceiling. In platinum, if you can reach F, reach F. The metal earns it."

**Natural 1ct in platinum (G-VS2):** [Browse certified G-VS2 emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — typically $2,800–$3,200 for 1ct GIA G-VS2.

**Natural 1ct in platinum (F-VS2):** [Browse F-VS2 certified emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&colorMin=F&colorMax=F&clarityMin=VS2&clarityMax=VS2&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — typically $3,300–$3,800 for 1ct GIA F-VS2.

**Lab 1ct in platinum (F-VVS1):** [Browse lab IGI emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — approximately $450–$600 for a 1ct IGI F-VVS1. Lab stones in platinum fully realize The Color Ceiling at a fraction of natural cost.

